Z||000002||SLYGUY||10-13-2001||02:32 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by btoth:<BR><B>The place I took mine to the labor cost was $750.  That was to install a new 2.8 long-block.  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I'm thinking of doing that exact same thing if/when my 2.8 goes in my 88GT. Don't get me wrong, my car runs fabulous and only has (gulp) 102K miles on it. I'hoping for at least 150K+ out of it, but that is the way I'll be going. <P>When I shop around for a 2.8 long block, where is the best place to start looking?<BR>Should I research engine rebuilders? <BR>I saw quite a few rebuilt long blocks with a reasonable guarantee at Kragen (Checker for you south paws).<P>Thanks again.<P>Sly||||reg||1
